/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nubels/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nubels/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nubels/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nubels/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nubels/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nubels/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nubels/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nubels/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-26T11:29:30Z","updated_at":"2025-06-26T11:29:30Z","body":"@AThousandShips Yes, it happens there, too. It seems to heavily depend on how the displays are arranged. After I changed the arrangement, the issue appeared again.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3008157425/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3477927878","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106555#issuecomment-3477927878","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106555","id":3477927878,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7PTPfG","user":{"login":"rlamprell","id":90906655,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwOTA2NjU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90906655?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rlamprell","html_url":"https://github.com/rlamprell","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rlamprell/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rlamprell/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rlamprell/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rlamprell/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rlamprell/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rlamprell/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rlamprell/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rlamprell/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rlamprell/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-02T12:36:08Z","updated_at":"2025-11-02T12:54:07Z","body":"I have this issue too - on (macos) godot4.5 release.  But, monitor arrangement (including which screen is the primary) does not seem to affect where the game window appears.  It will always jump to the display that does not have the Godot editor on it.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3477927878/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3776731734","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106555#issuecomment-3776731734","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106555","id":3776731734,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hHFpW","user":{"login":"ColinSORourke","id":44822820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODIyODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44822820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinSORourke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-21T08:14:13Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T08:21:40Z","body":"@rlamprell @nubels I have tested this on my MacOS with a 2nd monitor, and examined the code, and I believe this is Godot behaving as (currently) intended.\n\nMost (all?) Editor Windows store memory of positioning and size in the Project Metadata, and restore said positioning and size when they are reopened. The Position is stored not local to a specific screen, but as a \"global screen position\" and whenever possible, will restore to the screen it was on last. For example, in Project_Settings_Editor.cpp:\n\n```cpp\nvoid ProjectSettingsEditor::popup_project_settings(bool p_clear_filter) {\n\t// Restore valid window bounds or pop up at default size.\n\tRect2 saved_size = EditorSettings::get_singleton()->get_project_metadata(\"dialog_bounds\", \"project_settings\", Rect2());\n\tif (saved_size != Rect2()) {\n\t\tpopup(saved_size);\n\t} else {\n\t\tpopup_centered_clamped(Size2(1200, 700) * EDSCALE, 0.8);\n\t}\n```\n\nUpon very first launch, the Project Settings is popped up on the same screen as the Editor is currently, via popup_centered_clamped. Once closed, the ProjectSettings Window stores its current position and size to the Project Metadata, and in all future popups will attempt to restore that position and size, including screen arrangement. In my testing, I was not able to find any way to cause the very first opening of ProjectSettings to be on a different screen than the Editor itself. And in further testing, ProjectSettings always opened on the screen it was last closed on. \n\n<details>\n<summary>Detailed example</summary>\n<img width=\"563\" height=\"248\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d515c118-add3-449a-ae93-b43596a50946\" />\n\n> The issue seems to be the position that is passed to the Window::popup. The Rect2i of the first screen doesn't have the position and so it uses the next screen instead.\n\nThis is the intentional behavior for screen restoration. With the screen arrangement above, the featured code loops over:\n```\nScreen 0 usable rect: 0, 568, 3456, 1994\nScreen 1 usable rect: 3456, 62, 3840, 2098\n````\nX position 0 is the left edge of my screen arrangement.\nY position 62 is the top edge of my screen arrangement (right below 62 pixels of MacOS Header bar)\nY position 568 is the top edge of my laptop screen, as it is ~500 pixels below my extra monitor.\nX Position 3456 is the right of my laptop screen, and the left edge of my monitor.\n\nIf I launch Godot, open the Project Settings Window, and move it to the left edge of my laptop and close, the Window Position is saved in the Metadata as: \n```\n[dialog_bounds]\n\nproject_settings=Rect2(0, 1456, 1048, 476)\n```\nAppropriately placing it at the left edge of my Laptop. If I reopen the Project Settings Window, and move it to the left edge of my monitor, the position in the metadata becomes:\n```\n[dialog_bounds]\n\nproject_settings=Rect2(3458, 1138, 1048, 476)\n```\nAnd reopens correctly in the same position at the left edge of my monitor. \n</details>\n\nI would suggest this issue be closed unless:\n* Anybody can find a straightforward example of an Editor Window consistently returning to an incorrect position\n* Anybody can find a straightforward example of popup_centered_clamped behaving unintuitively\n* Or we want to leave this discussion up to consider if this behavior of always returning to a saved position should be changed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3776731734/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]